Philip Nee created KAFKA-16474:
----------------------------------

             Summary: AsyncKafkaConsumer might rapidly send out successive =
heartbeat causing partitions getting revoked
                 Key: KAFKA-16474
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16474
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: consumer
            Reporter: Philip Nee
            Assignee: Philip Nee


KAFKA-16389

We've discovered that in some uncommon cases, the consumer could send out s=
uccessive heartbeats without waiting for the response to come back.=C2=A0 t=
his might result in causing the consumer to revoke its just assigned assign=
ments in some cases.=C2=A0 For example:

=C2=A0

The consumer first sends out a heartbeat with epoch=3D0 and memberId=3D''=
=C2=A0

The consumer then rapidly sends out another heartbeat with epoch=3D0 and me=
mberId=3D'' because it has not gotten any response and thus not updating it=
s local state

=C2=A0

The consumer receives assignments from the first heartbeat and reconciles i=
ts assignment.

=C2=A0

Since the second heartbeat has epoch=3D0 and memberId=3D'', the server will=
 think this is a new member joining and therefore send out an empty assignm=
ent.=C2=A0=C2=A0

=C2=A0

The consumer receives the response from the second heartbeat.=C2=A0 Revoke =
all of its partitions.

=C2=A0

There are 2 issues associate with this bug:
 # inflight logic
 # rapid poll: In the KAFKA-16389 we've observe consumer polling interval t=
o be a few ms.=C2=A0=C2=A0



