> > define different DLQs for different data flows? This is especially
> > important when dealing with multiple source topics that have different
> > record schemas.
> >
> > 2.
> > Your DLQ payload value can either be the record value that failed, or a=
n
> > error string (such as "error during punctuate"). This is likely to caus=
e
> > problems when users try to process the records from the DLQ, as they ca=
n't
> > guarantee the format of every record value will be the same. This is ve=
ry
> > loosely related to point 1. above.
> >
> > 3.
> > You provide a ProcessorContext to both exception handlers, but state th=
ey
> > cannot be used to forward records. In that case, I believe you should u=
se
> > ProcessingContext instead, which statically guarantees that it can't be
> > used to forward records.
> >
> > 4.
> > You mention the KIP-1033 ProcessingExceptionHandler, but what's the pla=
n
