Yangkun Ai created KAFKA-16561:
----------------------------------

             Summary: Disable `allow.auto.create.topics` in MirrorMaker2 Consumer Config
                 Key: KAFKA-16561
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16561
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Yangkun Ai


While using MirrorMaker 2.0 (MM2), I noticed that the consumer used by the connector does not disable the ALLOW_AUTO_CREATE_TOPICS_CONFIG option. This leads to the possibility of a topic being immediately recreated if I attempt to delete it from the source cluster while MirrorMaker 2.0 is running. I believe that automatic creation of new topics in this scenario is unreasonable, hence I think it is necessary to explicitly disable this option in the code.



--
