Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-16562:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Install the ginkgo to tools folder
                 Key: KAFKA-16562
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16562
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


https://github.com/apache/yunikorn-k8shim/blob/master/scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh#L111

`run-e2e-tests.sh` install the ginkgo in the `GOBIN` folder. However, our `make e2e_test` assumes all tools are installed at yunikorn-k8shim/tools, and hence we can see `Command 'ginkgo' not found` error if we don't export the `GOBIN`.

It seems to me this jira should includes following changes.

1. move the ginkgo installation from run-e2e-tests to makefile. Let `make tools` install all required tools
