Hi, Kafka Team.
I am writing test code for the new rebalancing protocol proposed in KIP-848=
.

It works well in general code. However, it does not work properly when crea=
ting an EmbeddedBroker using KafkaTestKit.java.

=C2=A0
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
### Phenomena
 # Create a CombineBroker that acts as both controller and broker using Kaf=
kaTestKit.
 # Consumer do subscribe() and poll() to created Broker.=C2=A0
=C2=A0

At this time, the Consumer sends a HeartBeat Signal to the Broker successfu=
lly. However, it never receives a Partition Assigned response from the Brok=
er.
=C2=A0
### What is my broker configs?=C2=A0
!image-2024-04-30-19-19-12-316.png|width=3D530,height=3D228!
=C2=A0
### Actual Broker Config.
!image-2024-04-30-19-20-14-427.png|width=3D465,height=3D151!
I set controller.quorum.voters =3D 0@localhost:9093, but 0@0.0.0.0.0:0 is s=
etted.=C2=A0
Because of this codes ([https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/7c0a302c4da9d5=
3a8fddc504a9fac8d8afecbec8/core/src/test/java/kafka/testkit/KafkaClusterTes=
tKit.java#L305-L307)]
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
### My opinion.
I am not familiar with the broker's quorum, but it seems to be the problem.
=C2=A0
I expect that when the Consumer sends a poll request to the broker, the gro=
up coordinator broker assigns the topic/partition and then performs quorum =
for each epoch number.
=C2=A0
However, it seems to not work because the controller to vote is represented=
 as 0.0.0.0:0.
=C2=A0
This setting does not work well when applied to containers in docker-compos=
e.
Could this be the cause of the problem?
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
### Question
If {{controller.quorum.voters}} is set to {{0.0.0.0:0}} and i want to use c=
onsumer group rebalancing through KIP-848, what settings should be applied =
to the brokers and consumers?



